{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01HcA7Yat7vrRdW22avp8cQw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Here is a grounded summary of the v3 \"Mission Control\" planning trio session, with each claim tied to the member documents (Master Plan, Implementation Plan, Execution Log):\n\n## North Star (locked objective)\n- Turn the Anchor dashboard into a **durable mission-control for trio-driven R&D**, where every project is a thin, full-width row carrying an accurate, auto-generated summary.\n- Clicking any session expands a concise, **cached, in-place** summary â€” *when Â· what-was-asked Â· North-Star Â· clickable doc links Â· effort (tokens + time)* â€” never a separate \"no summary\" page.\n- Trio work runs as **persistent, isolated, server-side terminal sessions** managed like stacking windows (open / attach / minimize / kill-with-confirm), status-colored, and surviving disconnect â€” so launching a session feels like a real terminal.\n\n## Locked decisions (Stage 0/1 user gates)\n- **Terminal substrate = real ConPTY** (via `pywinpty`). This *consciously waives* Anchor's \"stdlib-only / no-native-assets\" rule **for the terminal subsystem only** â€” everything else stays stdlib, and the subsystem (and the dashboard) **degrades gracefully if `pywinpty` is absent**.\n- **Summaries = proactive background generation, cached.** Generated once (at discovery/rescan and right after a run completes); clicking shows a ready, cached summary in-place, with lazy \"generatingâ€¦\" only as a fallback.\n- **Concurrency isolation = git worktrees per session.** Each plan/research/build session gets its own isolated worktree so concurrent sessions can't dirty each other's trees.\n\n## Document set (provenance)\n- The frozen design is the **Master Plan**; the **Implementation Plan** is the Foreman-ready, wave-by-wave build plan; the **Execution Log** records the per-wave build/review history.\n\n---\n\n*Note: the bullets above are grounded strictly in the anchors surfaced from the member documents. Claims about specific module names, wave counts, or build status are not asserted here because they weren't present in the provided document anchors.*"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4310,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":92107,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2b02eee1-5b05-490e-9193-41a66397d48c","uuid":"de1f48c9-7afd-4ab0-9a4f-43e9f7e90446","request_id":"req_011CcJoG4BYXmpi8uFo6rfNU"}
